# decisions: A11Y-3, A11Y-4, A11Y-8, COL-12, DOC-1, DOC-2, FOC-1, FOC-6, OVL-13
# hunks:
#   FOC-1, FOC-6: the toast root's `outline-none focus-visible:border-ring
#     focus-visible:ring-[3px] focus-visible:ring-ring/50` halo goes; dropping `outline-none` lets
#     the single 2px `:focus-visible` outline `base.css` owns through.
#   COL-12: `ToastIcon` paints each type in its own status family — `success`, `info` and
#     `warning` gain an ink where upstream left them inheriting the body colour, and `error`
#     moves from the `destructive` FILL to `destructive-text`. The `-text` role is the one that
#     passes AA as ink on a `popover` surface, which is the pair A11Y-13 named in Batch 2.
#   NO HUNK, FLAGGED FOR MK — Base UI's `aria-hidden-focus` defect. For a `priority: "high"`
#     toast, `@base-ui/react@1.8.0` announces a visually hidden `role="alert"` clone in the
#     viewport and marks the VISIBLE root `role="alertdialog" aria-hidden="true"` so the
#     viewport's own polite region does not announce it twice — while leaving the root and its
#     action and close buttons in the tab order. Nothing tabbable may sit inside an `aria-hidden`
#     subtree, so axe reports a SERIOUS `aria-hidden-focus` violation on upstream's own
#     composition. It is NOT patched here: no decision row authorises it, and the only fix inside
#     this file is a DOM-mutating layout effect in a shipped component. It takes the shape Batch 3
#     used for Combobox's aria-hidden addon instead — `toast.test.tsx` exempts that one axe rule
#     for the high-priority state ALONE and pins the engine's exact shape beside it, so the
#     exemption fails as stale the day Base UI fixes it. Worth reporting upstream.
#   OVL-13: `ToastPortal` reads `useInternalThemeScope()` and wraps its children in a
#     `display: contents` element carrying that class.
#   A11Y-8: NO HUNK. Upstream already signals type with a shape as well as a colour — `ToastIcon`
#     renders a distinct lucide glyph per type, and the COL-12 hunk above only colours glyphs that
#     are already there. `toast.test.tsx` asserts the icon, so a future upstream that drops it
#     fails here.
#   A11Y-3, A11Y-4: NO HUNK. Base UI's `Toast.Viewport` IS the mounted-for-life polite region this
#     policy asks for — `role="region"`, `aria-live="polite"`, rendered by `Toaster` whether or
#     not a toast exists — and per-toast urgency is the manager's `priority: "high"`. Adding a
#     second region would announce every toast twice. `toast.test.tsx` asserts the region's shape.
#   cn: `import { cn } from "cn"` becomes `@vegastack/design` — our npm layer owns `cn` (DOC-2).
#   formatting: prettier reflow plus the `registry-stamp.mjs` provenance header (DOC-1); no
#               decision of their own.
